  {
    "who": "leon",
    "message": "Found it. The importer built **one giant `INSERT … VALUES (…),(…)` statement** for every point. Past roughly 20k points SQLite hits its limit and throws `too many SQL variables`.\n\nI changed it to a prepared statement inside a single transaction, which is both safe and fast:\n\n```ts\nconst insert = await db.prepareAsync(\n  'INSERT INTO track_points (lat, lon, ele, time) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)'\n)\nawait db.withTransactionAsync(async () => {\n  for (const p of points) {\n    await insert.executeAsync([p.lat, p.lon, p.ele ?? null, p.time])\n  }\n})\nawait insert.finalizeAsync()\n```\n\nAll 7 importer tests pass now, including the Tour du Mont Blanc sample (24,318 points) in about 1.8 s.",
    "messageId": "134c119d-9961-4cd5-9ec6-a4ed7c3a1ee8:leon",
